3 NOTE María Antonia Petronila Pérez Restrepo, lived in a time and place where clothes were shipped as merchandise to the viceroyalties aboard Spanish galleons. Wealthy ladies also kept up with the fashion being worn in Europe, observing
4 CONC  the costumed dolls that were sent, and having local seamstresses and tailors copy the models.
