1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maria Leocadia lived in a difficult transitional time when the role of woman was subdued to the impositions of her family, the husband, the Catholic Church, and the established traditions inherited from the Spanish
2 CONC  Conquistadores. Colonial society was just stabilizing. Many families were wary of their daughters’ suitors. Whenever women went out to shop in the market, or attend the religious services, they had to be accompanied, sometimes by
2 CONC  slaves. Many took refuge from their hardships in endless rosaries, as a way of escaping, as it was socially accepted and understood. Others, died during childbirth, due to the precarious conditions of the epoch. It was well looke
2 CONC d and even sought, to have as many children as possible, as not all reached their adulthood, and there was a need to pass on the lineage, and prosper as much as possible in this new brave world.
