3 NOTE María Leocadia Palacio Restrepo was a traveller between Abejorral, Manizales, Medellín… the so-called Paisa region. Her family, the Palacio, were thriving and multiplying so fast, that practically, they were part of the heart and 
4 CONC motor of the “Paisa Migration” moving from Antioquia, to what is now Caldas, and further to northern Tolima, participating in the early establishment of Líbano, Tolima.
