3 NOTE Joaquín was able to return triumphant after battling in the First Independence Wars in Colombia. However, he died of unexpected causes in a place close to his city, Manizales -known as La Ceja del Tambo-. His unexpected death alon
4 CONC g with the passing away of his elder brother Francisco, in battle, led to the sudden dementia of their mother, unable to cope with these 2 deaths, dying shortly afterwards. Peace in their tombs.
