1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===My Grandmother’s Grandfather Pedro Palacio=== by Viviana Ferreira Prada
2 CONT
2 CONT My third Great-grandfather Pedro Palacio, in the simplicity of his beautiful villa in Abejorral, Antioquia, where he would get up early for a breakfast of peto (white corn boiled until softened) with a splash of milk and pieces of
2 CONC  panela (hardened sugar cane product), freshly Colombian Mountain black coffee, that is, sweetened with panela, acompanied with eggs fried in butter, white paisa arepa (flat round white grits cake) served piping hot from the oven,
2 CONC  to be opened with the knife, in order to add butter and salt to it.
2 CONT
2 CONT I know this was Pedro’s favourite breakfast as his great-great-grandson, my father, referred he came from a long paisa line that used to start the day this way when they were established in houses, because when they were in the mu
2 CONC leteer or in the mining, the meal varied to an arepa,”calentao” (hot mixture of fresh white rice with the cooked red beans of the day before), and varied charcuterie.
2 CONT
2 CONT All this to make sure the man would be able to face the tasks of the day well "fed" according to the nutritional standards of the time, which nowadays with so much butter, bacon and charcuterie, would be sending us straight to a c
2 CONC ardiologist, since most of these ancestors invariably died of fulminant heart attacks between the fourth and fifth decades of their lives.
