1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marcelino Palacio Restrepo, the son of Don Francisco Palacio Guerra and María Teresa Restrepo, founders of Abejorral, was born and baptized on June 20, 1810 in Rionegro, Antioquia. He was the penultimate of 14 sibl
2 CONC ings, and his older sister turned 32 a few days after his birth and was already married, so he had several nieces and nephews his own age.
2 CONT
2 CONT He spent his childhood and adolescence in Abejorral. At the age of 19, he saw his mother go insane with grief over the death of two of her brothers who had gone to war in 1814, to the Cauca campaign, when Marcelino was 4 years old
2 CONC , so he never really knew them. It is said that he also joined the military (he was in Medellín in 1834) and campaigned on the coast before returning to his mother's house in Abejorral.
2 CONT
2 CONT His time in the military was brief, as when he was around 24 years old, his mother died and his father died at 27; both in Abejorral. He embarked on his journey to the south of Antioquia with a large part of his family and friends
2 CONC ; he lived for a time in Arma and another in Neira, where he contributed to its foundation.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mercedes, daughter of Joaquín Echeverri Díaz and Rosa Isaza Echeverri. His brothers-in-law were Melitón, Alejandro, Manuel, Mercedes, and Juan Pablo Echeverri. According to Polo Giraldo's research, he had 7 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken and translated to english  by his 4th great-grand niece,  Viviana Ferreira Prada from:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://raicespaisas.wordpress.com/2016/05/02/raices-paisas-quien-fue-don-marcelino-palacio/
