2 TITL Pedro Pablo Arango Ángel
2 NOTE Pedro Pablo Arango Ángel, my fifth grandfather, lived in a time where men lived in a region that was essentially agricultural and dedicated to mining. The difficulty of exercising agriculture in the high mountains then developed a
3 CONC n economy that became essentially commercial and mining, thus developing a culture of walkers, of muleteers, which produced a private economy of monoproduction and export of gold, accompanied by an incipient subsistence of agricul
3 CONC tural production that was born around small villages.All this produced at the same time a financially and sustainably solid social class. 
